    rdamd:P30117 "illustrated by Graham Ingels; written by Al Feldstein with Ray Bradbury" ;
    rdamd:P30137 "\"Guided by EC historian John Benson's research on EC release dates, we have attempted to present the stories in this book in the order in which they originally appeared, as follows: \"Hook, line, and stinker!\" in Vault of Horror #26, August-September 1952; A little stranger! in Haunt of Fear #14, July-August 1952; Squash...anyone? in Tales from the Crypt #32, October-November 1952; A grim fairy tale! in Vault of Horror #27, October-November 1952; Chatter-boxed! in Haunt of Fear #15, September-October 1952; Private Performance in Crime SuspenStories #14, December 1952-January 1953; None but the lonely heart! in Tales from the Crypt #33, December 1952-January 1953; We ain't got no body! in Vault of Horror #28, December 1952-January 1953; Sugar 'N spice 'N... in Shock SuspenStories #6, December 1952-January 1953; Nobody there! in Haunt of Fear #16, November-December 1952; Hail and heart-y! in Crime SuspenStories #15, February-March 1953; There was an old woman! in Tales from the Crypt #34, February-March 1953; Pickled pints! in Vault of Horror #29, February-March 1953; Horror we? How's bayou?in Haunt of Fear#17, January-February 1953; This wraps it up! in Tales from the Crypt #35, April-May 1953; Notes to you! in Vault of Horror #30, April-May 1953; Pipe down! in Haunt of Fear #18, March-April 1953; The handler in Tales from the Crypt #36, June-July 1953; One good turn... in Vault of Horror #31, June-July 1953; Sucker bait! in Haunt of Fear #19, May-June 1953; The rover boys! in Tales from the Crypt #37, August-September 1953; Funereal disease! in Vault of Horror #32, August-September 1953; Thump fun! in Haunt of Fear #20, July-August 1953; Mournin' mess in Tales from the Crypt #38, October-November 1953; Strung along! in Vault of Horror #33, October-November 1953; An off-color heir in Haunt of Fear #21, September-October 1953.\" -- page facing title page." ;
    rdamd:P30156 "Sucker Bait and other stories" ;
    rdamd:P30176 "Fantagraphics Books" ;
    rdamd:P30182 "xiii, 201 pages : black and white illustrations, 27 cm." ;
    rdamo:P30001 rdact:1049 ;
    rdamo:P30002 rdamt:1007 ;
    rdaxd:P00018 "isbn-1606996894",
        "isbn-9781606996898" .

